  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram shows electric field lines near three points: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Z\"></span>. The field lines are closer together near <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Z\"></span> and further apart near <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which statement about the magnitude of the electric field at these points is correct?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">The electric field is strongest at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and weakest at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Z\"></span>.</li><li data-label=\"B\">The electric field is equally strong at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Z\"></span> because the field is uniform.</li><li data-label=\"C\">The electric field is strongest at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Z\"></span> and weakest at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>.</li><li data-label=\"D\">The electric field is zero at point <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> because the lines curve.</li></ol>"
  },
